# Build context for zk/operator/Dockerfile.
#
# The awkward part is `target/`: it is 23 GB and must not be sent, EXCEPT for the guest ELFs, which
# are the one build output the image genuinely needs. They are compiled outside the image — see the
# Dockerfile header for why — and they are 4.7 MB sitting inside 1.3 GB of intermediate build
# state, so the re-includes below name the release directory's direct children and nothing under
# them. Docker applies every pattern and the last match wins; `*` does not cross a `/`, so
# `release/deps/whatever.rlib` stays excluded by the blanket rule above.
#
# `cargo prove build --docker` and the plain path land in different directories, so both are named.

**/target
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Runtime credentials and machine-local overlays must never enter either production image's build
# context. Examples are tracked and safe; every other dotenv file is deployer-owned input.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

!zk/program/target/elf-compilation/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/trustgraph-program-v2/target/elf-compilation/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/weighted-program/target/elf-compilation/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/composition-program/target/elf-compilation/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/nostr-program/target/elf-compilation/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*

!zk/program/target/elf-compilation/docker/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/trustgraph-program-v2/target/elf-compilation/docker/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/weighted-program/target/elf-compilation/docker/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/composition-program/target/elf-compilation/docker/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*
!zk/nostr-program/target/elf-compilation/docker/riscv64im-succinct-zkvm-elf/release/*

# The frontend and indexer are not part of the Rust operator build, and `packages/` is 3.6 GB.
# The production indexer image re-includes only its own package, its workspace dependency, and the
# small shared frontend libraries its handlers import directly. Build artifacts and node_modules
# remain excluded by the blanket rules above.
packages
!packages/
packages/*
!packages/indexer/
!packages/indexer/**
!packages/eas-offchain-client/
!packages/eas-offchain-client/**
!packages/frontend/
packages/frontend/*
!packages/frontend/lib/
!packages/frontend/lib/**

# NOT excluded, however tempting: `research/`. `zk/prover` has two dev-dependencies with paths into
# it, and cargo resolves dev-dependencies even for a plain `cargo build` — a missing path
# dependency fails at manifest load, forty minutes into a release.

# Local state and generated artifacts. `.demo` and `.trustgraph` in particular can hold a request
# journal and a submitter's working files, which have no business in an image.
.demo
.trustgraph
.docker
broadcast
cache
out
deployments/**/dev*
repos
**/*.log
